## Summary
Ukraine's top anti-corruption court has set bail at approximately $450,000 for Irina Mudraya, a former aide to President Zelensky who stands accused of money laundering. The brief report covers the outcome of her bail hearing.

## Key Points
- Ukraine's top anti-corruption court set bail at roughly $450,000 for Irina Mudraya
- Mudraya is a former aide to Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky
- She faces accusations of money laundering
- The case is being handled by Ukraine's specialized anti-corruption court system


